          "alt": "The marking scheme's own print of its answer to 2021 HL Q9(c)(ii), as the State Examinations Commission set it: CALCULATE 25/243 / 0.103 (12), in two boxed routes: letting x be the moles of N₂ that reacted, initial, change and equilibrium moles of N₂, H₂ and NH₃ (9.0 − x, 27.0 − 3x, 2x mol) (3); 2x = 6 ⇒ x = 3, so 6 mol N₂, 18 mol H₂ and 6 mol NH₃ (3); divided by 10.0, 0.6 mol/l N₂, 1.8 mol/l H₂ and 0.6 mol/l NH₃ (3); Kc = 0.6² over 0.6(1.8)³ = 25/243 / 0.103 (3); or the same per litre from 0.9 mol/l N₂ and 2.7 mol/l H₂, with marks at each step; [No mixing and matching of contents of boxes above.]",
