    section: "A", questionRef: "2023 HL Q3(c)(iii)",
    stem: "A student carried out an experiment to measure the heat of reaction (ΔH) for the neutralisation of hydrochloric acid by sodium hydroxide according to the following equation. HCl (aq) + NaOH (aq) → NaCl (aq) + H₂O (l) In the experiment the student used an expanded foam polystyrene cup with a plastic lid through which a thermometer and a plastic stirrer were inserted, as shown on the right. The student first added 50 cm³ of 1.0 M HCl solution at room temperature to the polystyrene cup and then quickly added 50 cm³ of 1.0 M NaOH solution, also at room temperature, and having lowered the lid stirred the mixture while observing the thermometer. The temperature of the mixture rose rapidly by 6.8 K and then began to fall very slowly.",
