    section: "B", questionRef: "2024 HL Q10(c)(ii)",
    stem: "Rusting of iron involves several different reactions that take place in the presence of moist air. The mass of an iron object and its overall volume increase because of these rusting reactions occurring on the surface of the object. One of the reactions is described by the following balanced chemical equation: 4Fe + 3O₂ → 2Fe₂O₃ The mass of an iron object increased by 1.92 g as a result of this reaction.",
