          "alt": "The marking scheme's own print of its answer to 2019 HL Q2(c)(iv), as the State Examinations Commission set it: (iv) CALCULATE: 300 to 315 cm³ / 0.300 to 0.315 litres (8); boxed, density = mass over volume ⇒ 0.8 = mass over 2.9 ⇒ m = 0.80 × 2.9 = 2.32 g (✓), 2.32 over 46* = 0.0504 moles ethanol used (✓); then either ⇒ 0.0504 × 26 over 100 = 0.013104 actual mol ethene (✓) and 0.013104 × 24,000 = 300 - 315 cm³ ethene / 0.013104 × 24.0 = 0.300 - 0.315 litres ethene (✓), or 0.0504 × 24, 000 = 1200 - 1210 cm³ ethene in theory / 0.0504 × 24.0 = 1.21 litres ethene in theory (✓) and ⇒ 1200 × 26 over 100 = 300 - 315 cm³ ethene / ⇒ 1.21 × 26 over 100 = 0.300 - 0.315 litres ethene (✓); the rounding note; \"Four ticks: mass, moles, percentage, volume or mass, moles, volume, percentage. Award 3 marks for each of the first two correct ticks and 1 mark for each remaining correct tick. (3 + 3 + 1 + 1)\"; or, taking the percentage first, 2.9 × 26 over 100 = 0.754 cm³ ethanol (✓), m = 0.80 × 0.754 = 0.6032 g (✓), 0.6032 over 46* = 0.013104 moles ethanol used (✓) / m = 0.80 × 2.9 = 2.32 g (✓), 2.32 × 26 over 100 = 0.6032 g (✓), 0.6032 over 46* = 0.013104 moles ethanol used (✓); then 0.013104 × 24,000 = 300 - 315 cm³ ethene / 0.013104 × 24.0 = 0.300 - 0.315 litres ethene (✓); \"Do not penalise if volume of 22.4 litres or 22 400 cm³ used.\", the rounding note and the same tick rule.",
