          "alt": "The paper's own print of 2019 HL Q3(d): \"3. To determine the relative molecular mass (Mr) of compound X, a volatile liquid, a small volume of the pure liquid was vaporised in a suitable container. The atmospheric pressure at the location was obtained using a smart phone barometric sensor, as shown below.\"; then \"(d) Calculate, correct to the nearest whole number, the relative molecular mass of X, given that 0.22 g of X occupied a volume of 76 cm³ at a pressure of 1.011 × 10⁵ Pa and a temperature of 99 °C. (15)\"; below, a smart phone showing a barometer headed \"Atmospheric Pressure\", its dial marked 850 to 1100 hPa with weather symbols and its needle just past 1000, and the reading \"1011 hPa\".",
