          "srcHash": "47070c3950494097a3f3e3c708d21c98",
          "alt": "The marking scheme's own print of its answer to 2019 HL Q3(d), as the State Examinations Commission set it: CALCULATE: 88 [88 or 89] (15); boxed, n = pV over RT / pV = nRT (5); n = 1.011 × 10⁵ × 76 × 10⁻⁶ over 8.3 × 372.15 / 1.011 × 10⁵ × 76 × 10⁻⁶ = n × 8.3 × 372.15 (3) [Use of Kelvin essential here] [Apply slip error once to pressure not in Pa and/or volume not in m³.]; n = 2.49 × 10⁻³ moles [2.48 × 10⁻³ – 2.49 × 10⁻³ moles] (3); or, boxed, p₁V₁ over T₁ = p₂V₂ over T₂ / V₁ over T₁ = V₂ over T₂ (5); 101.1×76 over 372.15 = 101.325×V₂ over 273.15 / v₂ = 101.1×76×273.15 over 101.325×372.15 / v₂ = 76×273.15 over 372.15 / V₂ = 55.65 – 55.7 cm³ (3) [Use of Kelvin essential here]; n = 55.66 over 22400 = 2.48 × 10⁻³ moles [2.48 × 10⁻³ – 2.49 × 10⁻³ moles] (3) [Treat a mathematical slip incorrect power of ten in answer.]; and, boxed, n = m over Mr / Mr = m over n / Mr = 0.22 over 2.49 × 10⁻³ (2); Mr = 88.4 = 88 [88 or 89]* (2); \"Allow relative molecular mass of X not rounded to whole number. Do not penalise where relative molecular mass of X is labelled g.\"",
          "attribution": "SEC Leaving Certificate Chemistry 2019 Higher Level — © State Examinations Commission",
          "solution": true,
