          "src": "/exam-figures/chemistry/markbank/chemistry-2019-HL-scheme-q6c-iii.png",
          "srcHash": "dc0100280383b1b67665ca220384d53f",
          "alt": "The marking scheme's own print of its answer to 2019 HL Q6(c)(iii), as the State Examinations Commission set it: CALCULATE: –6,277.7 kJ mol⁻¹ (17), in four boxed routes: ΔH = ΣΔHformation products – ΣΔHformation reactants = –6,296 kJ (3) + (–5,716) (3) + (–438.0) kJ (3) – (105.4) kJ (3), or = –12,450 kJ (9) – 105.4 kJ (3), and = –12,555.4 kJ mol⁻¹ (3), ΔHcombustion = –12 555.4 ÷ 2 = –6,277.7 kJ mol⁻¹ (2); or ΔHcombustion = ΣΔHformation products – ΣΔHformation reactants = –3,148 kJ (3) + (–2,858) kJ (3) + (–219.0) kJ (3) – (52.7) kJ (3), or = –6,225 kJ (9) – 52.7 kJ (3), and ΔHcombustion = –6,277.7 kJ mol⁻¹ (5); or 16C + 16O₂ → 16CO₂ ΔH = –6,296 kJ (3), 20H₂ + 10O₂ → 20H₂O ΔH = –5,716 kJ (3), 2Pb + O₂ → 2PbO ΔH = –438.0 kJ (3), 2(C₂H₅)₄Pb → 16C + 20H₂ + 2Pb ΔH = –105.4 kJ (3), giving 2(C₂H₅)₄Pb + 27O₂ → 16CO₂ + 20H₂O + 2PbO ΔH = –12,555.4 kJ mol⁻¹ (3) and ΔHcombustion = –12,555.4 ÷ 2 = –6,277.7 kJ mol⁻¹ (2); or 8C + 8O₂ → 8CO₂ ΔH = –3,148 kJ (3), 10H₂ + 5O₂ → 10H₂O ΔH = –2,858 kJ (3), Pb + ½ O₂ → PbO ΔH = –219.0 kJ (3), (C₂H₅)₄Pb → 8C + 10H₂ + Pb ΔH = –52.7 kJ (3), giving (C₂H₅)₄Pb + 13½O₂ → 8CO₂ + 10H₂O + PbO ΔHcombustion = –6,277.7 kJ mol⁻¹ (5); then \"Mixing and matching from different boxes not acceptable. Equations not essential, however:\" and two Final Answer rules: \"8CO₂ + 10H₂O + PbO → (C₂H₅)₄Pb + 13½O₂ ΔH = 6,277.7 kJ is worth 14 marks only with this equation / 6,277.7 kJ is worth 5 marks if accompanied by any other equation or by no equation\" and \"16CO₂ + 20H₂O + 2PbO → 2(C₂H₅)₄Pb + 27O₂ ΔH = 12,555.4 kJ is worth 12 marks only with this equation 12,555.4 kJ is worth 3 marks if accompanied by any other equation or by no equation\".",
