          "alt": "The marking scheme's own print of its answer to 2019 HL Q11(b)(ii), as the State Examinations Commission set it: (ii) CALCULATE: 48% First correct tick 6, each other correct tick 2 marks (12); two boxed routes in moles. The first: Let x = number of moles of Br₂ (or Cl₂) produced; 2BrCl (g) ⇋ Br₂ (g) + Cl₂ (g); Initially 0.200 mol, 0 mol, 0 mol; Change – 2x mol, + x mol, + x mol; Equil 0.200 – 2x, x mol, x mol / Equil 0.200–2x over 5, x over 5, x over 5 mol/l, A = (✓); (Kc =) 0.220 = x² over (0.200–2x)², in three forms, / 0.12x² + 0.176x – 0.0088 = 0, B = (✓); square rooting both sides ⇒ 0.469 = x over 0.200–2x ⇒ 0.0938 – 0.938x = x ⇒ x = 0.0484 mol / solving quadratic ⇒ x = 0.0484 mol, C = (✓); 2x over 0.2 × 100 = 0.0968 over 0.2 × 100 = 48.4% ⇒ 48%* or 49%* decomposed / now working in moles per litre: 0.048 × 2 moles of BrCl decomposed ⇒ 0.0192 moles/l of initial 0.04 moles/l BrCl decomposed ⇒ 0.0192 over 0.04 × 100 = 48.4% ⇒ 48%* or 49%* decomposed, D = (✓). The second: Let x = number of moles of BrCl decomposed; Equil 0.200 – x, ½x mol, ½x mol; (Kc =) 0.220 = x² over 4(0.200 – x)², in three forms, / 0.12x² + 0.352x – 0.0352 = 0; x = 0.0968 mol; x over 0.2 × 100 = 48.4% ⇒ 48%* or 49%* decomposed / in moles per litre, 0.0194 over 0.04 × 100 = 48.5% ⇒ 48%* or 49%* decomposed; A to D ticked as before.",
