    section: "B", questionRef: "2018 HL Q5(d)(iv)",
    stem: "The radioisotope carbon–14 emits beta particles and has a half‐life of 5730 years. A piece of fossilised yew, from a tree that was alive about 6000 years ago, was excavated from Boora Bog, Co. Offaly. When a tiny fragment of it was analysed, it was found to contain 1.5 × 10¹² carbon–14 atoms.",
