          "alt": "The marking scheme's own print of its answer to 2018 HL Q5(d)(iv), as the State Examinations Commission set it: 7.0 × 10⁻¹¹ g of carbon–14 originally (6); three boxed routes separated by \"or\": 3.0 × 10¹² ÷ 6.0 × 10²³ = 5.0 × 10⁻¹² moles of carbon–14 originally (3), 5.0 × 10⁻¹² × 14* = 7.0 × 10⁻¹¹ g originally (3); mass of carbon–14 in a.m.u. originally = 3.0 × 10¹² × 14* = 4.2 × 10¹³ (3), 4.2 × 10¹³ ÷ 6.0 × 10²³ = 7.0 × 10⁻¹¹ g originally (3); mass of one carbon–14 isotope = 14* × 1.66 × 10⁻²⁷ = 2.324 × 10⁻²⁶ kg (3), 3.0 × 10¹² × 2.324 × 10⁻²⁶ = 7.0 × 10⁻¹⁴ kg originally / 7.0 × 10⁻¹¹ g originally (3); then \"[*Using 12 instead of 14 here is more than a slip.]\" and \"[Allow more exact mass of carbon-14 taken from Formulae and Tables booklet, page 83.]\"",
