    section: "A", questionRef: "2016 HL Q1(a)",
    stem: "To determine the concentration of ethanoic acid in a sample of vinegar, 25.0 cm³ of the vinegar were diluted to 250 cm³ and then the diluted vinegar was titrated with a previously standardised solution which contained 1.20 g of sodium hydroxide in 500 cm³ of solution. On average, 18.75 cm³ of the diluted vinegar were required to neutralise 25.0 cm³ of this sodium hydroxide solution. The equation for the titration reaction is: CH₃COOH + NaOH → CH₃COONa + H₂O",
    questionText: "Describe in detail the procedures involved in measuring a 25.0 cm³ sample of the vinegar and diluting it using deionised water to exactly 250 cm³.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed"}, totalMarks: 15,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "use 25 cm³ pipette (burette)", marks: 9, contextNote: "MEASURE: any three of these, (3) each: \"ANY THREE: (3 × 3)\". The scheme sets its fourth point for a pipette and, after it, for a burette: the one used.", openList: true, group: {"claimMax":3,"perOption":3,"options":["use 25 cm³ pipette (burette)","previously rinsed with deionised (distilled, pure) water","and previously rinsed with vinegar (solution it will contain, sample)","pipette: read at eye-level / read bottom of meniscus / bottom of meniscus on the mark / allow drainage time / last drop to remain (not to be shaken out, blown out) / drain under gravity / touch (tip, tap) pipette against wall of flask","burette: read at eye-level / jet (part below tap) full / vertical / read bottom of meniscus"]} },
    { id: "r-2", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "transfer to 250 cm³ volumetric flask", marks: 6, contextNote: "DILUTE: any two of these, (3) each: \"ANY TWO: (2 × 3)\". The scheme adds: [Award marks for reference to ‘bottom of meniscus’ once only in (a).]", openList: true, group: {"claimMax":2,"perOption":3,"options":["transfer to 250 cm³ volumetric flask","previously rinsed with deionised (distilled, pure) water","fill with deionised water until bottom of meniscus is on mark","stopper and invert flask a number of times / stopper and mix contents thoroughly"]} },
    ],
