          "alt": "The marking scheme's own print of its answer to 2014 HL Q1(f), as the State Examinations Commission set it: \"54 – 54.4% (3)\"; boxed, \"Hydrated = 2.50 g/250 cm³ / 10 g l⁻¹\", \"Anhydrous = 1.14 – 1.15 g/250 cm³ / 4.58 – 4.6 g l⁻¹\", \"Water = 1.35 – 1.36 g/250 cm³ / 5.4 – 5.44 g l⁻¹\", \"=> 1.35/1.36 over 2.5 × 100 / 5.4/5.44 over 10 × 100 = 54% (3)\". Then \"VALUE OF x: 6.9 – 7 (6)\" and a table of two columns, headed \"Formula mass of Na₂CO₃ = 106\" and \"Formula mass of H₂O = 18\", \"OR\" between them, five rows of two routes, each two steps (3) each. Row one: \"Na₂CO₃ content = 4.6 g l⁻¹ [4.5792 – 4.6]\", \"H₂O content = 10 – 4.6 = 5.4 g l⁻¹ [5.4 – 5.4208]\", 5.4 over 4.6 = 18x over 106 (3), \"x = 6.9 – 7 (3)\"; and \"Na₂CO₃ content = 1.15 g /250 cm³ [1.14 - 1.15]\", \"H₂O content = 2.5 – 1.15 = 1.35 g /250 cm³ [1.35 - 1.36]\", 1.35 over 1.15 = 18x over 106 (3), \"x = 6.9 – 7 (3)\". Row two: the same contents, then 4.6 over 106 : 5.4 over 18 / 0.043 : 0.3 (3), \"= 1 : 6.9 – 7 (3)\"; and 1.15 over 106 : 1.35 over 18 / 0.0109 : 0.075 (3), \"= 1 : 6.9 – 7 (3)\". Row three: \"Hydrated form: 10 g l⁻¹ = 0.0432 M\", Formula mass = 10 over 0.0432 / 231.5 (3), x = 231.5−106 over 18 = 6.9 – 7 (3); and \"Hydrated form: 2.5 g /250 cm³ = 0.0108 mol\", Formula mass = 2.5 over 0.0108 / 231.5 (3), x = 231.5−106 over 18 = 6.9 – 7 (3). Row four: Mr(hyd) over 106 = 10 over 4.6* / Mr(hyd) = 230.4 [230.4 -231.5] [*4.5792 – 4.6] (3), x = 230.4−106 over 18 = 6.9 – 7 (3); and Mr(hyd) over 106 = 2.5 over 1.15* / Mr(hyd) = 230.4 [230.4 - 232.5] [*1.14 – 1.15] (3), x = 230.4−106 over 18 = 6.9 – 7 (3). Row five: mass(water) over 106 = 5.4 over 4.6 [5.4 – 5.4208][4.5792 –4.6] / mass(water) = 124.4 [124.4 – 125.5] (3), x = 124.4 over 18 = 6.9 – 7 (3); and mass(water) over 106 = 1.35 over 1.15 [1.35 - 1.36][1.14 - 1.15] / mass(water) = 124.4 [124.4 – 125.5] (3), x = 124.4 over 18 = 6.9 – 7 (3). Below: \"[Reminder: second 3 may be awarded consequentially.]\"",
