          "alt": "The marking scheme's own print of its answer to 2013 HL Q11(b), as the State Examinations Commission set it: \"CALCULATE: 11.28 (11.3) (12)\"; boxed, \"7 g of NH₄OH = 7 ÷ 35 = 0.2 mol ⇒ 0.2 M NH₄OH (3)\"; then two routes, each boxed: \"[OH⁻] =\" the square root of \"1.8 × 10⁻⁵ × 0.2\" \"/ 1.9 × 10⁻³ (3)\", \"pOH = – log 1.9 × 10⁻³ = 2.72 (2.7) (3)\", \"pH = 14 – 2.72 (2.7) = 11.28 (11.3) (3)\"; and \"[OH⁻] =\" the same square root \"/ 1.9 × 10⁻³ (3)\", \"[H⁺] =\" 1 × 10⁻¹⁴ over that square root \"/\" 1 × 10⁻¹⁴ over 1.9 × 10⁻³ \"/ 5.3 × 10⁻¹² (3)\", \"pH = – log 5.3 × 10⁻¹² = 11.28 (11.3) (3)\".",
